{"key":"hf4-apphy2-mcq-001-v1","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"A","final_answer":"1.5 × 10⁵ Pa","working":"For an ideal gas in a rigid, sealed container, the volume and amount of substance are constant. According to Gay-Lussac's Law, P1 / T1 = P2 / T2, where temperature must be expressed in kelvins. \nT1 = 27°C + 273.15 = 300.15 K ≈ 300 K. \nT2 = 177°C + 273.15 = 450.15 K ≈ 450 K. \nSolving for P2 gives P2 = P1 × (T2 / T1) = (1.0 × 10⁵ Pa) × (450 K / 300 K) = 1.5 × 10⁵ Pa.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":407,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":407,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":546,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":220,"reasoningTokens":326},"totalTokens":953,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":326,"promptTokenCount":407,"candidatesTokenCount":220,"totalTokenCount":953,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":407}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":220}]},"reasoningTokens":326,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":4410,"keyed_label":"A"}
{"key":"hf4-apphy2-mcq-001-v2","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"D","final_answer":"−273°C","working":"The relationship between pressure P and Celsius temperature T is linear: P = m*T + P_0. The slope is m = (160 kPa − 120 kPa) / (127°C − 27°C) = 40 kPa / 100°C = 0.4 kPa/°C. Setting P = 0 gives 0 = m*T + P_0, or T = T_1 − P_1 / m = 27°C − (120 kPa / 0.4 kPa/°C) = 27°C − 300°C = −273°C.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":412,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":412,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":584,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":187,"reasoningTokens":397},"totalTokens":996,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":397,"promptTokenCount":412,"candidatesTokenCount":187,"totalTokenCount":996,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":412}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":187}]},"reasoningTokens":397,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":4660,"keyed_label":"D"}
{"key":"hf4-apphy2-mcq-001-v1","kind":"mcq","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"A","final_answer":"1.5 × 10⁵ Pa","working":"For a fixed amount of ideal gas in a rigid sealed container, volume is constant, so pressure is proportional to absolute temperature. Convert Celsius to kelvin: T1 = 27 + 273.15 = 300.15 K and T2 = 177 + 273.15 = 450.15 K. Using P1/T1 = P2/T2, solve for P2 = P1 × T2/T1 = (1.0 × 10⁵ Pa) × (450.15 K / 300.15 K) ≈ 1.5 × 10⁵ Pa.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":460,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":204,"cacheReadTokens":256},"outputTokens":486,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":164,"reasoningTokens":322},"totalTokens":946,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":460,"completion_tokens":486,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":256,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":204,"total_tokens":946,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":256},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":322}},"reasoningTokens":322,"cachedInputTokens":256},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":5447,"keyed_label":"A"}
