{"key":"hf4-apphy2-mcq-001-v3","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"C","final_answer":"627°C","working":"For an ideal gas in a rigid sealed container, the volume and number of moles are constant, so by the ideal gas law, pressure is directly proportional to absolute temperature (P ∝ T). The initial temperature in Kelvin is T₁ = 27°C + 273 = 300 K. For the pressure to triple (P₂ = 3P₁), the absolute temperature must also triple: T₂ = 3 × 300 K = 900 K. Converting back to Celsius: T₂ = 900 - 273 = 627°C.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":376,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":376,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":555,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":168,"reasoningTokens":387},"totalTokens":931,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":387,"promptTokenCount":376,"candidatesTokenCount":168,"totalTokenCount":931,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":376}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":168}]},"reasoningTokens":387,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":4181,"keyed_label":"C"}
