{"key":"hf4-apphy2-mcq-001-v3","kind":"mcq","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"C","final_answer":"627°C","working":"For a fixed amount of ideal gas in a rigid sealed tank, volume and moles are constant. Gay-Lussac's law gives P/T = constant when T is absolute. Thus P2/P1 = T2/T1. Given P2 = 3P1, T2 = 3T1. Converting 27°C to kelvins: T1 = 27 + 273 = 300 K. Therefore T2 = 3 × 300 K = 900 K. Converting back to Celsius: T2 = 900 - 273 = 627°C.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":426,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":170,"cacheReadTokens":256},"outputTokens":340,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":153,"reasoningTokens":187},"totalTokens":766,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":426,"completion_tokens":340,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":256,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":170,"total_tokens":766,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":256},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":187}},"reasoningTokens":187,"cachedInputTokens":256},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":3994,"keyed_label":"C"}
